# A turn still running on a pane 30 columns wide, as claude 2.1.259 draws it.
# The vendor composes its spinner row as a glyph, a gerund, an ellipsis, and
# then a parenthesis holding the elapsed time and a detail after it. That
# parenthesis is a tail it drops from the right as the pane narrows, and at
# this width the whole of it is gone.
#
# There are no hooks under this on purpose. A reader is at the screen because
# the hooks have stopped -- an agent interrupted with Escape, or one nobody has
# heard from -- and the mode footer claude draws while it works is on this
# screen too, so the row alone has to tell a turn that is running from one that
# is over.
print ● Finagling… thinking
print ──────────────────────────────
print ❯
print ──────────────────────────────
print   ⏵⏵ auto mode on
# The turn runs until whoever is driving this scenario ends it.
sleep 600000
